# --- Python bytecode, everywhere (S109) ---
# This was enumerated per-directory SEVEN times and never globally, which is a whitelist
# wearing an ignore rule's clothes: .claude/ was the eighth Python directory and fell
# through, so gate.py's cache landed in git and re-dirtied the muster card on every run.
# Note *.py[cod] also matches .pyd (a Windows extension module) - none are tracked today;
# if one is ever vendored it needs an explicit un-ignore.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- Windows widget (Tauri / Node / Rust) ---
windows-widget/node_modules/
windows-widget/dist/
windows-widget/src-tauri/target/
windows-widget/src-tauri/Cargo.lock

# --- Linux receiver (Python) ---
linux-receiver/.venv/
linux-receiver/__pycache__/
linux-receiver/**/__pycache__/
linux-receiver/*.egg-info/
linux-receiver/.pytest_cache/

# --- Linux dashboard (Python) ---
linux-dashboard/.venv/
linux-dashboard/__pycache__/
linux-dashboard/**/__pycache__/
linux-dashboard/*.egg-info/
linux-dashboard/DEVNOTES.md

# --- Linux converter (Python) ---
linux-converter/.venv/
linux-converter/__pycache__/
linux-converter/**/__pycache__/
linux-converter/*.egg-info/

# --- OS / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log

# --- Secrets / local config overrides ---
*.local.toml
.env
.claude/settings.local.json

windows-converter/__pycache__/
# backend_parity.py output. Regenerated by every run, so a committed copy would go stale and
# then read as the record. The record is the CHANGELOG entry and the session closeout.
windows-converter/backend_parity.json
# Probe page renders: ~1 MB each and byte-reproducible from the source PDF at the dpi the
# probe README records. The model's OUTPUTS (glm-*.md) are the evidence and stay tracked.
prototypes/glm-ocr-probe/*.png

# S78: the glass detector's own bytecode
observability/__pycache__/
prototypes/__pycache__/
prototypes/**/__pycache__/

# --- Wiki profiles: the private layer (S107) ---
# The repo is PUBLIC on GitHub. A profile's personal content lives only in the
# gitignored *.private.md layer; the tracked layer carries role + working agreements.
# Enforced mechanically by `.claude/skills/wiki/wiki.sh check` (a tracked private
# file is a measured red).
wiki/profiles/*.private.md

# --- .agents/: Codex's runtime skills mirror (B2, signed S108) ---
# Divergent by design and resolved only by Codex's harness; never by Claude Code.
# Tracked canonical skills live in .claude/skills/.
.agents/

# --- The private layer (S108, Rab's correction 2026-08-24) ---
# Both models share this filesystem; the only boundary that ever mattered is the PUSH.
# Evidence that must be readable locally but never world-readable lives here. The bus
# carries the pointer + digest; these bytes never leave the machine.
# The ignore boundary follows the OWNERSHIP boundary that single-writer already sets.
coordination/private/*
!coordination/private/README.md
codex/private/

# relay-gate's stable cross-process advisory lock. It must persist by pathname while waiters
# may still hold the same file, but it is runtime state rather than relay evidence.
coordination/.relay-gate.lock

# dumps/ — Rab bought the disk so evidence stops evaporating (2026-08-26).
# The BYTES are local and heavy; the LEDGER is tracked and light. Git history therefore
# preserves the RECORD of every dump even after the dump itself is gone — which is the
# whole reason the split is exactly here. Tracked bytes would also leave the tree
# permanently dirty and break close.sh's '0 uncommitted'.
dumps/*
!dumps/README.md
!dumps/LEDGER.md
!dumps/dump.sh
!dumps/.gitattributes
